1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:02,610
(Howard:)...with indestructible
Kryptonian perspiration.

2
00:00:05,692 --> 00:00:07,322
Booyah.

3
00:00:09,362 --> 00:00:12,452
(Sheldon:)Superman would have taken his uniform
to a Kandorian dry-cleaner...

4
00:00:12,616 --> 00:00:14,746
(Sheldon:)...before he left the bottle.

5
00:00:15,410 --> 00:00:19,660
Kandorian dry-cl...? I give up. You can't have
a rational argument with this man.

6
00:00:21,333 --> 00:00:24,543
(Howard:)Hey, isn't that the guy who won
the MacArthur genius grant last year?

7
00:00:25,337 --> 00:00:27,507
(Howard:)No, not all at once.

8
00:00:27,672 --> 00:00:30,802
- Then how?
- Leonard.

9
00:00:32,135 --> 00:00:33,965
(Howard:)Now Raj.

10
00:00:35,472 --> 00:00:37,392
(Howard:)Now Sheldon.

11
00:00:39,059 --> 00:00:41,899
- I didn't get a good look. Can I go again?
- No.

12
00:00:42,062 --> 00:00:45,062
- That's David Underhill. So what?
- So what?

13
00:00:45,232 --> 00:00:48,772
(Sheldon:)His observation of high-energy positrons
has provided the first evidence...

14
00:00:48,944 --> 00:00:51,024
(Sheldon:)...for the existence
of galactic dark matter.

15
00:00:51,196 --> 00:00:54,616
(Leonard:)I have two words for you.
The first is "big," the other's "whoop."

16
00:00:55,075 --> 00:00:59,025
It is a big whoop. Made almost all the work
you've done completely useless.

